# A guard on a register a vector load overwrote: the load is its
# definition, so the store runs on at most the CTA's 64 threads, not on
# all 64 as when only the earlier `mov %r3, 0` was seen; its sectors per
# request and the CTA's global store bytes are bounds.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/vector_def.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_vector_def( // block 64×1×1 | per CTA: global load 512 B, store <= 256 B; param load 512 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p1 st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // <= warp * × lane * | exec <= 64/CTA | global store [8·%tid.x + param_0] sectors/req <= 9 (ideal <= 4){{$}}
